{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"d7537c7c47440a70574e952071d2f1d21e5962ec87e78e9e0846fa5501e3721a","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_1b14f3a66bcd467b0af568281577115d1cb025d2c1bf79c7c754d107cddd734e","overall_assessment":"The primary policy violation is the breach of double-blind anonymity due to the inclusion of author names, affiliations, and emails. While the data usage is largely compliant given the synthetic nature of most datasets, the lack of explicit licensing information for the authors' code and the absence of any ethical or broader impact discussion are notable omissions, though less critical in the context of the 2017 submission standards.","paper_id":"B1MRcPclx","paper_identity_sha256":"0b5fb6e854d23af2de1f9c8cb687c8412500f2bdf9aadb8673687f1007fb7320","prompt_identity_sha256":"5e578c5e2c669f8fa71b515d8b33a491e274594a2ce7d31d2830a0e6bb7aa65a","raw_response_sha256":"0e7c8101604ebc2073a71d55b2ea7ba1930d7c3d2d9c4184901b5b3e67debd5a","request_identity_sha256":"5c2d5b89eec98ca44028b7f894e0c56a8527399e106f8ed8b470d2371a362807","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a dedicated section on ethics, fairness, or potential harms. While the work focuses on synthetic and semi-synthetic datasets (bAbI, DSTC2) for question answering and dialog, there is no discussion of how the model might be misused, potential biases in the training data, or the impact of automated dialog systems on user trust. Given the 2017 venue context, a formal ethics statement was not always mandatory, but the absence of any broader ethical consideration regarding the deployment of such systems is a limitation.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-024","SRC-025"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes the bAbI story-based QA dataset, bAbI dialog dataset, and the DSTC2 dataset. The bAbI datasets are synthetic, generated by templates, and thus do not raise privacy concerns regarding personally identifiable information (PII). The DSTC2 dataset is a real-world dialog dataset from the Second Dialog State Tracking Challenge. The paper cites the source (Henderson et al., 2014) and notes that it was transformed by Bordes and Weston (2016). There is no explicit statement regarding data licensing, consent, or anonymization procedures for the DSTC2 data, although its use in a public benchmark challenge implies standard academic usage rights. No privacy violations are evident in the text.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists the authors' names (Minjoon Seo, Sewon Min, Ali Farhadi, Hannaneh Hajishirzi) and their institutional affiliations (University of Washington, Allen Institute for Artificial Intelligence, Seoul National University) on the first page. It also provides direct email addresses for the authors. This violates the double-blind review policy typically enforced at ICLR, as it allows reviewers to identify the authors and their affiliations, potentially introducing bias.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper presents a novel model, the Query-Reduction Network (QRN), with distinct architectural contributions such as the specific update gate mechanism and parallelization strategy. The references are properly cited, and the text does not appear to duplicate content from other sources without attribution. There is no evidence of plagiarism or dual submission within the provided text.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-034"],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement or a checklist for responsible AI, which were not standard requirements for ICLR submissions in 2017. However, the lack of discussion on the societal implications of automated question answering and dialog systems is a gap. The paper mentions the use of TensorFlow (Abadi et al., 2016) for implementation, which is open-source, but does not specify the license under which the authors' own code or model weights are released, nor does it provide a link to a repository. This limits the reproducibility and clarity of compliance with open-science practices.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"af218df5b7a6c6b3b7285a70e34276003f84a578a8a439c547d075787d66019f","paper_id":"B1MRcPclx","paper_ordinal":10,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"0e7c8101604ebc2073a71d55b2ea7ba1930d7c3d2d9c4184901b5b3e67debd5a","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1MRcPclx","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"227fc6efe69abf1667b1b1fe3a72f015b5076eda7cda013e53acc1f393e228e2","request_identity_sha256":"5c2d5b89eec98ca44028b7f894e0c56a8527399e106f8ed8b470d2371a362807","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v2","usage":{"completion_tokens":890,"prompt_tokens":20273,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":21163},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"5c2d5b89eec98ca44028b7f894e0c56a8527399e106f8ed8b470d2371a362807","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v1"}